\f0\fs24 \cf2 The display cabinet in the Red Room is much more than a decorative piece: it\'92s a love story carved into wood, a concentration of symbols, history, and exceptional craftsmanship. Look closely at the initials carefully engraved: LI BO, for Lina Borromeo, and BA VA, for Giuseppe Bagatti Valsecchi. An elegant tribute to their union. But the heart of the piece lies at the center: the family crests intertwine, merging past and identity.\
On the left, the proud eagle and lilies of the Bagatti Valsecchi family. On the right, the motto \'93Humilitas\'94 in Gothic script \'96 symbolizing virtue and devotion \'96 and the famous knot with three circles, emblematic of the indissoluble bond between the Sforza, Visconti, and Borromeo families. Every detail comes from a well-thought-out design: the Bagatti Valsecchi brothers sketched two distinct drafts, one for the frame and another for the heraldic group. Bringing these designs to life was Innocente Cattaneo, a skilled craftsman, who with extraordinary precision created this wooden masterpiece. A piece of furniture that tells a story of love, heritage, and beauty, waiting to be discovered.\
}